Q: Discord.js how to add role to a specific user ID? A: <p>The issue seems to be the lack of asyncronous handling. Besides that the <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/ClientEvents:Interface#ready" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ready</code> event is deprecated</a>, your code lacks of any <code>await</code>: this could lead to have variables treated as <code>undefined</code> since some function has yet to return that object.</p>
<p>As per today, the <code>get</code> method can't be found neither:</p>
<ul>
<li>in the <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/GuildManager:Class" rel="nofollow noreferrer">docs of <code>GuildManager</code></a> (returned by <code>bot.guilds</code>),</li>
<li>in the <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/RoleManager:Class" rel="nofollow noreferrer">docs of <code>RoleManager</code></a> (returned by <code>guild.roles</code>),</li>
<li>and neither in the <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/GuildMemberManager:Class" rel="nofollow noreferrer">docs of <code>GuildMember</code></a> (returned by <code>guild.members</code>);</li>
</ul>
<p>It is, however, documented the <code>fetch</code> method instead, which returns a <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/Guild:Class#fetch" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Promise&lt;Guild&gt;</code></a>, a <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/RoleManager:Class#fetch" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Promise&lt;Role&gt;</code></a> and a <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/Guild:Class#fetch" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Promise&lt;GuildMember&gt;</code></a> respectively.</p>
<p>So, your code should look like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>bot.on('clientReady', () =&gt; {
    // To clarify further, I'll comment each line with the representing classes
    // Client.GuildManager.fetch()
    const guild = await bot.guilds.fetch(GUILD_ID);
    // Guild.RoleManager.fetch()
    let role = await guild.roles.fetch(ROLE_ID);
    // Guild.GuildMemberManager.fetch()
    let user = await guild.members.fetch(USER_ID);
    // GuildMember.GuildMemberRoleManager.add()
    user.roles.add(role);
});
</code></pre>
<p><strong>N.B.</strong> in this simple example there are no null checks nor any validation, but keep in mind that, for example, <a href="https://discord.js.org/docs/packages/discord.js/14.27.0/RoleManager:Class#fetch" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>RoleManager.fetch</code> could also return <code>null</code></a>.</p>

Q: Spring 3 MVC: Issue binding to list form fields on submit A: <p>I think you will need to write PropertyEditorSupport for your class. Following is the example for your reference.</p>

<pre><code>public class SampleEditor extends PropertyEditorSupport {

private final SampleService sampleService;

public SampleEditor(SampleService sampleService, Class collectionType) {
    super(collectionType);
    this.sampleService = sampleService;
}

@Override
public void setAsText(String text) throws IllegalArgumentException {
    Object obj = getValue();
    List list = (List) obj;
    for (String str : text.split(",")) {
        list.add(sampleService.get(Long.valueOf(str)));
    }
}

@Override
public String getAsText() {
    return super.getAsText();
}
</code></pre>

<p>}</p>

<p>In controller, you should bind it using @InitBinder as follows:</p>

<pre><code>@InitBinder
protected void initBinder(HttpServletRequest request, WebDataBinder binder) {
    binder.registerCustomEditor(List.class, "list", new SampleEditor(this.sampleService, List.class));
}
</code></pre>

<p>Hope this will solve your problem.</p>
